    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d219">

                <pb facs="0316" n="248" sameAs="frus:frus1914-20v01/pg248"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">763.72112/359a</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to President Wilson
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-09-28">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">September 28, 1914</hi>.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Mr. President</hi>: I enclose a draft of
                    telegram to the American Ambassador at London, in accordance with your direction
                    this morning.<anchor n="6" xml:id="d219-f1"/>
                </p>
                <p>I confess I am not satisfied with it, because there seems so much to say which is
                    not said. I hope you will please indicate any suggestions you may have as to
                    changes.</p>
                <p>Very sincerely yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d219-a1.xml" xpointer="d219-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d219-f1" n="6" xml:id="d219-f1-content">
                <p>For telegram as sent, see <ref target="frus1914Supp#pg_232">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Foreign Relations</hi>, 1914, supp., p.
                    232</ref>.</p>
            </note>
